{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWavyLine"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The trill-sound attribute group includes attributes used to guide the sound of trills, mordents, turns,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shakes, and wavy lines. The default choices are:","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwavyline\/trillsound"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWavyLine\/trillSound"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"trillSound"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTrillSound","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLTrillSoundV"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLWavyLineV10trillSoundAA08MXLTrillF0Vvp","role":"symbol","title":"trillSound"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"trillSound","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLTrillSoundV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTrillSound","text":"MXLTrillSound","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Start-Note = “upper” trill-step = “whole” two-note-turn = “none” accelerate = “no” beats = “4”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Second-beat and last-beat are percentages for landing on the indicated beat, with defaults of 25 and 75","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"respectively.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For mordent and inverted-mordent elements, the defaults are different:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default start-note is “main”, not “upper”. The default for beats is “3”, not “4”. The default for second-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"beat is “12”, not “25”. The default for last-beat is “24”, not “75”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWavyLine":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwavyline","role":"symbol","title":"MXLWavyLine","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWavyLine","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLWavyLine","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Wavy lines are one way to indicate trills and vibrato. When used with a barline element, they should always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have type=“continue” set. The smufl attribute specifies a particular wavy line glyph from the SMuFL Multi-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"segment lines range.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLWavyLine","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTrillSound":{"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLTrillSound","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltrillsound","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The trill-sound attribute group includes attributes used to guide the sound of trills, mordents, turns,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shakes, and wavy lines. The default choices are:","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text